### Release 36: more pages, more data, every page positive

- **Positive pages**: a search page never says what we lack. A page whose own list is empty shows the cars ready to book now and **Request this exact car**; the checks refuse copy that says "not available", "we don''t have" or "we don''t offer".
- **Popular cars**: a car with more than its share of the requests (Program settings, Demand steering: 25% by default) is placed lower in Trending (no higher than 6th), its page says **Popular** with similar cars first, and the search pages list it after the others. A pin still leads.
- **Car figures**: every car and vehicle page shows what the free sources give, each with its source: the manufacturer''s price, production years and plants (Wikidata), dimensions (NHTSA vPIC, Canada), recall campaigns (NHTSA and Transport Canada), the parts owners complain about most (NHTSA), charging, equipment, and ratings out of 10 with how each is worked out (fuel economy, performance, space, crash safety, recall record, parkability). The seo-data workflow loads them weekly; a curated CSV adds the manufacturer''s colours, prices and equipment.
- **Parking**: place, event and airport pages list the parking lots, garages and streets with parking nearby (OpenStreetMap).
- **Events**: **Marketing** > **Event pages** lists the Toronto and GTA events with a "Rent a car for" page. Add an event, or set its dates once the organiser announces them; until then the page says the months it is usually held. Sales sees the same list on its Marketing page.
- **Turo searches**: five landing pages for people searching Turo cancellations, deposits, fees, damage and missed handovers. They describe our own process and say CarmaCars is not affiliated with Turo.
- **GPS tracker**: its page (/gps-tracker) and a short section on the search pages, from Program settings (name, prices, features, details; off hides both).
- **Airports**: a page for Pearson and Billy Bishop: the car delivered to the terminal at the standard delivery price.
- **Renting vs owning**: a page per popular model year (and the nearest cities) with the monthly cost of owning, line by line with sources, against our monthly rate. The financing rate and term, kilometres, depreciation and cleaning are Program settings; insurance and parking figures are added with their source.
- **Languages**: the landing, event and airport pages in 18 languages (French, Punjabi, Mandarin, Cantonese, Arabic, Urdu, Tagalog, Spanish, Portuguese, Italian, Tamil, Farsi, Korean, Russian, Hindi, Gujarati, Vietnamese, Polish) at carmacars.ca/fr/... The seo-i18n workflow translates the templates once; a language is in search and named to Google only once 90% of its text is translated (Program settings).
- **Reviews**: real reviews show on every car page and search page with their source. **Reviews** > **Add a customer review** enters one that came another way (Turo, an earlier platform, a text, a call, email, in person, Google): the first name and last initial, the source, the date, the rating, the customer''s words exactly as received, and a screenshot if you have one. Never write or change a review for a customer. Hide one only for cause.
- **Sitemaps**: two more files, the new page families and the language versions (with each page''s languages), each with its own dates.

> Good to know: The Cantonese pages are translated by a person (the translation model has no Cantonese): until then they stay out of search.
