4. Post it on Facebook, open the new listing and copy its address. Back on **Today**, press **Posted** and paste the address. **Let go** frees a claim you will not post.
5. Press **Renewed**, **Updated** or **Taken down** when you do those on Facebook.

## Words to use

Nothing a buyer reads says "rent", "rental" or "for rent". Every listing keeps the line "Daily and weekly bookings only, not for sale" and the price is for one day. The kit and the replies already follow this.

## The auto-reply

**Auto-reply for this listing** has the steps and the text, with your listing''s own link. While posting, scroll to **Auto replies** (or **Meta AI replies**), turn it on, replace the draft with the text, then publish. It only answers the first "Is this available?".

## The inbox

1. Open facebook.com/marketplace/inbox, the Selling tab, oldest first.
2. Use **Inbox replies for this car** only: price, availability, requirements, deposit, delivery, send your number. One message per reply, at most two to someone who does not answer.
3. Then **Log an inbox session**: the chats, the replies and every number, one per line (name, phone, car code). Each new number is a lead credited to you, with a call-back task within 15 minutes.

## Your own Claude

**Your Claude in Chrome** has the instructions to paste into Claude in your own Chrome, and the **Academy lesson** that teaches them. Claude follows the same rules: the kit''s words and the templates only, it stops at any Facebook security check or CAPTCHA and tells you, it never types a password, and it logs every post in your Marketing tab.

> Watch out: Stop and tell the Admin if Facebook removes a listing or restricts your account. Do not appeal and do not post it again.

## Event pages

Below Marketplace, **Event pages** lists the Toronto and GTA events with a "Rent a car for" page. Press **Add an event** for a new one, or **Edit** to set its dates once the organiser announces them, with the organiser''s page as the source. Share an event page in your posts in the weeks before it.',
  '<p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Sales</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b>. You post CarmaCars cars on Facebook Marketplace from your own Facebook profile, answer the Marketplace inbox, and log what you did. The numbers you collect are leads credited to you.</p><section class="gd-task" id="marketing-on-facebook-marketplace-never-the-same-ad-twice" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Never the same ad twice</h2><p class="gd-p">Each car can have up to 5 live listings across the team (the owner&#39;s own listing included). Every listing is a different <b class="gd-ui">copy variant</b>: its own title, its own description wording, its own photo order and its own cover photo. When you claim a car, its variant is yours until you take the listing down or it lapses: no one else can post that copy. You can have one listing of a car at a time.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A claim you do not post within a day lets go by itself.</li><li>A listing ends 30 days after you posted or renewed it, unless you renew it.</li><li>The Admin sees who posted what, with the listing&#39;s address.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="marketing-on-facebook-marketplace-today" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Today</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Today</b> lists your work in this order: <b class="gd-ui">Take down</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Update the price</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Post it</b> (a car you claimed), then <b class="gd-ui">Renew</b> and new <b class="gd-ui">Post</b> items, up to your posts and renewals for the day (4 by default).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On a <b class="gd-ui">Post</b> item press <b class="gd-ui">Claim variant</b> with its number. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Kit</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The kit shows every field of facebook.com/marketplace/create/vehicle in order, each with <b class="gd-ui">Copy</b>, your variant&#39;s description and tracked link, and the photos in your order. Press <b class="gd-ui">Download the photos (ZIP)</b>: 01 is your cover. <b class="gd-ui">With scenes (ZIP)</b> takes the car&#39;s marketing set instead (its photos in other scenes, made on its listing).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Post it on Facebook, open the new listing and copy its address. Back on <b class="gd-ui">Today</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">Posted</b> and paste the address. <b class="gd-ui">Let go</b> frees a claim you will not post.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Renewed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Updated</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Taken down</b> when you do those on Facebook.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="marketing-on-facebook-marketplace-words-to-use" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Words to use</h2><p class="gd-p">Nothing a buyer reads says &quot;rent&quot;, &quot;rental&quot; or &quot;for rent&quot;. Every listing keeps the line &quot;Daily and weekly bookings only, not for sale&quot; and the price is for one day. The kit and the replies already follow this.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="marketing-on-facebook-marketplace-the-auto-reply" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The auto-reply</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Auto-reply for this listing</b> has the steps and the text, with your listing&#39;s own link. While posting, scroll to <b class="gd-ui">Auto replies</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Meta AI replies</b>), turn it on, replace the draft with the text, then publish. It only answers the first &quot;Is this available?&quot;.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="marketing-on-facebook-marketplace-the-inbox" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The inbox</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open facebook.com/m